  "articleBody": "It's easy to get excited about new kitchen tile, but some common missteps can really derail a project. One big one is skipping proper surface prep. If your subfloor isn't clean, level, and free of loose bits, your new tiles won't have a stable base, leading to cracks or popping. Always ensure the area is spotless and even before you start. Another frequent issue is using the wrong adhesive for your tile type and location. Different tiles and areas require specific glues, and an incorrect choice can mean your tiles won't bond correctly and could shift or come loose. Don't guess here; confirm the right product. Ignoring expansion gaps is another big one. Tiles expand and contract with temperature changes, and if they don't have room, they can buckle or crack. A professional knows where and how to leave these crucial gaps. Finally, rushing the cure time can be disastrous. Grout and adhesive need specific times to set properly before any foot traffic or heavy use. Cutting this short can compromise the entire installation. If you're unsure about any of these steps, especially with complex patterns or wet areas, a professional like HH Remodeling LLC can make sure it's done right the first time.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
